<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kertajaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned c. 1194–<a href="/years/1222">1222</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kertajaya was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri Kingdom</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pararaton">Pararaton</a> he quarrelled with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> and Buddhist clergy, who turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ken-arok">Ken Arok</a>, ruler of Tumapel. Ken Arok defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ganter">Battle of Ganter</a> in 1222 and founded the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a>.</p></div>
